        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0335" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00 Nanking/206</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Embassy to the
                            Department of State</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide Memoire</hi></p>
                <p>As the Secretary of State is no doubt aware, His Majesty’s Minister at Peking is
                    keeping in close touch with his United States and Japanese Colleagues, in order
                    to secure a satisfactory settlement of the Nanking incident.</p>
                <p>This constant interchange of views and information on the latest developments
                    between the three Ministers appears to afford sufficient guarantee that none of
                    their Governments will authorize the conclusion of any agreement for the
                    settlement of the incident, the terms of which have not previously been fully
                    discussed and concurred in by their respective Representatives at Peking.</p>
                <pb facs="0336" n="228" xml:id="pg228"/>
                <p>His Majesty’s Government trust that the Government of the United States share
                    their view as to the advisability of continuing to act on these lines.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1927-07-25"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">July 25, 1927</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
